 that snape  didn't get attacked by remus and the  whomping will of that fateful day  harry's father realized that their  so-called prank could be the end of  snape and so james called it off  of course that one good deed doesn't  excuse james for all his other bad ones  in that memory we also see james using a  spell to hang snape upside down  we get that he was unkind to snape but  his bullying behavior didn't stop there  fans of the book will know that james  was pretty unkind to other students too  he used to regularly hex them james even  made someone's head double in size  in fact he had such a reputation for it  lily described him as an arrogant toe  rag in the books  we get a feel for the history behind  severus and lilly's friendship when we  watch snape's memories in the deathly  hallows part two  they connect over their magical ability  before they even get to hogwarts but we  don't understand  the depth of their relationship from the  films or how their friendship ended  sure there's the moment snape calls lily  when he's embarrassed about her standing  up for him but in the deathly hallows  book we learn why  lily finished their friendship once and  for all it was down to his death eater  friends  lily could see that snape had chosen his  way and she'd chosen hers  in snape's memories in the film we also  see lily's first meeting with james  she smiles at him as they introduce  themselves to each other after they've  been sorted into gryffindor  it gives the impression that lily and  james were friends from the get-go  but actually as any fan of the books  will know lily was not a fan of james  nor his friends  it wasn't until james got his act  together for the final year of hogwarts  that lily started to like him  he was head boy and she was head girl oh  and in the books  they first met on the hogwarts express  in the movies it's a mystery why  wormtail was chosen as the potter's  secret keeper  after all surely sirius would have been  a much better 