y hallows  novel remus plans to abandon his wife  and unborn child to join harry  it's not because he isn't dedicated to  his family it's because he's terrified  of the repercussions of a werewolf  having a baby with a human  and he doesn't want to bring shame on  them fortunately harry talked remus into  going home  the prisoner of azkaban film completely  omits any mention of how sirius escaped  from jail  it's a seriously impressive feat given  that the prison is so closely guarded by  dementors  but we do learn in the third book how  sirius got away  he explains that he starved himself for  months and got thin enough to squeeze  through the bars  that explains why he looked so skinny in  the film but why didn't the dementor  sense his presence  because he was filled with hope about  tracking down worm tail  and the dementors can't detect hope  of course we know from harry's  eavesdropping session in the prisoner of  azkaban movie  that sirius was falsely imprisoned for  supposedly finishing off wormtail and  leading voldemort to his dear friends  james and lily but what we don't learn  in the film is that sirius also took the  wrap for wormtail's other evil actions  in the book we discovered that on the  night of their confrontation  wormtail causes an explosion that ended  the lives of 13 muggles  we know from the movie that sirius was  unfailingly loyal to james and lily but  it's only fans of the book who could  know that james was just as dedicated to  sirius  at the end of their fifth year at  hogwarts sirius ran away from his awful  death eater family  and the potter family offered him refuge  taking him into their home  it's not just serious that james gave  shelter to though he also financially  supported remus after they left school  because no one would give a werewolf a  job jk rowling revealed this indication  of what a good man james was  despite his wayward youth just say that  i'm used to it right now  we see how vicious the whomping willow  is in both the chamber of secrets and  prisoner of azkaban movies and we just  take it for granted that there'd be an  aggressive tree in the grounds of  hogwarts  but the books actually explain why the  willow is there and it's all down to  remus  when dumbledore let him study at the  school despite the fact that he was a  werewolf  the headmaster planted the whomping  willow to give remus safe passage to the  shrieking shack  remus is also responsible for the  formation of the marauders map  and the marauders themselves but we  wouldn't know this from watching the  films  in the prisoner of azkaban novel remus  reveals that when his friends discovered  he was a werewolf  they did something that made his  transformations not only bearable but  the best times of his life  they became anna mad guy prongs the stag  pad foot the dog and wormtail the rat  were created  they invented the map so they could  sneak around as animals and not get  caught  which of these secrets do you think most  deserves to have been included in the  movies  be sure to sound off in the comments  section and hit that like button if you  want to see a prequel movie all about  the marauders school days  thanks for watching
 

